{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6dxsdx6sfrz4rqjxwcogerf7ysehj7446yy3didguwtav5wf6eea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases complete. Summary:\n\n**Phase A — builds.** C: `cd c_src/build && cmake .. && cmake --build .` → `c_src/build/driver`. Rust: `cd translation && cargo build --release` → `translation/target/release/driver`. The Rust crate compiled without errors on the first attempt; no compile fixes were needed.\n\n**Phase B/C — 20 differential tests** in `translation/tests/differential.rs`, each comparing stdout, stderr *and* exit status. The program is tiny (`scanf(\"%d\")` then a loop printing `i` and `2i`), so I enumerated input classes from the two branch points: whether `scanf` converts, and whether `x > 0`. Covered: empty, whitespace-only, `x=0` (the `i < x` boundary), single item, every matching-failure form (`abc`, `.5`, `-`, `+`, `--3`, `- 3`, NUL, `\\xff`), whitespace skipping across newlines, trailing junk (`0x10` → 0, `1e3` → 1), only-first-number-read, leading zeros, and the out-of-range integer paths.\n\n**Two real mismatches found and fixed** (documented in `translation/ERRORS.md`):\n\n1. **SIGPIPE / exit status.** With stdout closed early, C died by signal (status 141) but the Rust exited 0 — the Rust runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main`, so the failing write returned `EPIPE`, which the translation discards. Fixed by restoring `SIG_DFL`. This is exactly the failure mode the brief warned about: a stdout-only test would have passed.\n\n2. **Over-consumption of stdin.** The translation read via `io::stdin()`'s 8 KiB `BufReader`, draining the whole descriptor; C leaves the remainder, because glibc repositions a seekable stream to the *logical* stream position at exit. Fixed with unbuffered one-byte `read(2)` calls plus `lseek(0,-1,SEEK_CUR)` to emulate `scanf`'s single `ungetc`. I measured C's exact consumption per input class first and matched it — notably, on `-abc` the sign stays consumed and only `'a'` is pushed back.\n\n**Behaviours preserved rather than \"fixed\":** a failed `scanf` silently leaves `x` at `0` (no diagnostic, exit 0); and out-of-range input saturates at `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` then truncates to `int`, so `2147483648` → `INT_MIN` (no output) while `4294967299` → `3` (three lines).\n\n**Phase D.** Both build warning-free; `cargo test` passes 20/20 in both debug and release; no test is `#[ignore]`d or skipped; `c_src/` sources are untouched (only the required `build/` directory added). A supplementary randomized sweep of 600 inputs found 0 mismatches.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: `x = 2147483647` and the signed overflow of `j` (needs `x > 2^30`) are not verified by execution — they'd take hours and emit tens of GB. The translation uses `wrapping_add` to match gcc's lowering of that UB, and I verified loop counts up to 70000 exactly; that gap is recorded in `ERRORS.md` rather than papered over."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":51179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be183f3d-7512-49cc-8e7a-bf8317017019","uuid":"f86880de-65aa-4531-9714-6173fab889c0","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:28:27.876Z"}
